VERSION "LiveWire S2 Del Mar (2024, S2DM) - Secondary CAN (DLC tap) - community reverse-engineered v0.1"

// ============================================================================
// LiveWire S2 Del Mar - Secondary CAN bus signal database
// ============================================================================
// Vehicle : 2024 LiveWire S2 Del Mar (S2DM), VIN odo ~2510 mi at capture time
// Bus     : SECONDARY CAN, tapped at the Data Link Connector [91] (JST MWT 6-way)
//           DLC pinout (from H-D EDM): pin2=W/R=CAN-H, pin5=W/BK=CAN-L,
//           pin3=BK/GN=ground, pin4=R/Y=accessory power, pins 1&6 = N/C
// Bitrate : 500000 (classical CAN, 11-bit standard IDs)
// Members : BCM (gateway/network mgr), TCU, IM, DLC   [per H-D EDM topology]
// NOTE    : PEU/RESS/EHCU/IMU/RHCM/LHCM are on PRIMARY CAN, NOT visible here.
//           Motor/inverter/BMS broadcast data is on primary; reach it via UDS
//           through the BCM gateway (0x7Ex addresses seen on this bus).
//
// Byte convention in comments: D1..D8 = SavvyCAN export columns = CAN data[0..7]
// In DBC start-bit terms below, big-endian (Motorola) signals are used where the
// capture showed BE multi-byte values.
//
// Verification method (general):
//   Isolated single-action captures, differential analysis (before/during/after),
//   cross-checked across multiple independent captures. Timestamps were logged as
//   0 (ESP32RET/A0 export bug) so sequence-order + rider action logs were used as
//   the time axis. Where a physical reference existed (odometer mi, indicated
//   speed), decoded values were checked against it.
//
// Confidence tags in comments: [CONFIRMED] cross-verified >=2 ways;
//   [STRONG] single clean capture, physically consistent; [TENTATIVE] needs more data
// ============================================================================
//
// ===== FRAME INTEGRITY (E2E) - CRACKED =======================================
// ~36 high-rate frames carry AUTOSAR-style END-TO-END protection:
//   D7 = ALIVE COUNTER, 6-bit, increments 0..63 then wraps to 0.
//   D8 = CRC-8 / SAE-J1850  (poly 0x1D, init 0xFF, xor-out 0xFF, refin/refout=NO)
//        computed over D1..D7 (the 7 preceding bytes, INCLUDING the counter).
//        This is the AUTOSAR E2E Profile-1 CRC, applied to the raw 7 payload bytes
//        WITHOUT a Data-ID prefix - a J1850-CRC E2E-like scheme, simpler than
//        textbook Profile 1 (no per-message Data ID folded into the CRC).
//   Python: crc=0xFF; for b in D1..D7: crc^=b; 8x{ crc=((crc<<1)^0x1D)&0xFF if
//           crc&0x80 else (crc<<1)&0xFF }; checksum = crc ^ 0xFF
//   PROTECTED IDs (D7=alive ctr, D8=CRC): 0x122 124 126 128 12A 131 133 134 152
//     154 15A 160 161 162 163 164 180 181 182 183 184 185 186 187 188 189 1A6
//     1A7 1C7 1C9 260 322 324 35A 3C8 562.  Verified 100% frame match. Use it to
//     VALIDATE a decode (a mis-aligned read fails CRC) and to detect dropped frames
//     (counter gaps).
//   UNPROTECTED IDs (D7 & D8 CONSTANT padding, no per-frame integrity): 0x136 138
//     261 262 326 328 332 334 338 33A 33C 33E 354 392 394 395 3C4 3C6 3CA 3CC 3CE
//     3CF. A few carry an internal counter mid-frame (0x3C4 D3, 0x3C6 D5) but no CRC.
//     NOTE: even the fast 0x326 (wheel speeds) is unprotected - protection tracks the
//     authoring module / signal criticality, not the frame rate.
//
// ===== ID-MAP PROVENANCE =====================================================
// The S2 does NOT reuse the combustion-Harley CAN map: 0x383 (radio), 0x521 (speed),
// 0x530, 0x540/0x541 (engine), 0x544 (throttle), 0x5C1 (clock) are ALL ABSENT - a
// purpose-built EV ID map, not a warmed-over platform DBC (despite shared module
// architecture). Some frames are ALLOCATED-BUT-EMPTY reserved slots: 0x394 / 0x3CA /
// 0x3CF read all-zero; 0x328 / 0x3CC are sentinel-filled (0xFF/0xFE) placeholders.
// Stack is AUTOSAR (per the E2E CRC-8/J1850); the IM is a Harley first-party module,
// software-versioned via Harley SIP (e.g. LiveWire Instrument Module 02.02.00). No
// public community CAN documentation exists for the LiveWire - this DBC is novel.
// ============================================================================


// ---- 0x122 (290) : IMU 3-AXIS ACCELEROMETER (lean/tilt) - CONFIRMED ----------
// [RESOLVED - 3-AXIS ACCELEROMETER, see BO_ below] 0x122 is not six independent bytes - it is
//   THREE 16-BIT PAIRS with an offset-binary (signed) encoding:
//     D1:D2, D3:D4, D5:D6, each with value - 32768 giving a signed number.
//   Evidence: D1, D3, D5 take only ~2 values each (~128, ~128, ~97) i.e. they are
//   HIGH BYTES sitting near the 0x8000 signed-zero point, while D2, D4, D6 sweep
//   247/241/223 distinct values as low bytes. Decoded that way the ranges are
//   sensible: D1:D2 = -56..+137, D3:D4 = -253..+37, D5:D6 = -7865..-7654.
//   WHAT THEY ARE NOT: correlated against speed, motor load, battery flow and
//   acceleration over 2469 paired samples, every r is between -0.06 and +0.08 -
//   i.e. no relationship to any vehicle dynamic we have decoded. Specifically NOT
//   battery power (that hypothesis was tested and failed).
//   These are the highest-resolution unexplained channels on the bus and the most
//   likely place for something significant still to be hiding.
//   HISTORICAL NOTE: earlier passes examined D2/D4/D6 as standalone bytes, which is
//   why they looked like noise - the pairing was the missing piece.
BO_ 290 IMU_ACCEL_122: 8 IM
 SG_ accel_lateral      : 7|16@0+ (1,-32768) [-32768|32767] "count" Vector__XXX
 SG_ accel_longitudinal : 23|16@0+ (1,-32768) [-32768|32767] "count" Vector__XXX
 SG_ accel_vertical     : 39|16@0+ (1,-32768) [-32768|32767] "count" Vector__XXX
// [CONFIRMED] 0x122 = 3-AXIS ACCELEROMETER (IMU), gatewayed from primary CAN. Three
//   signed 16-bit channels, offset-binary (physical value = raw - 32768):
//     D1:D2 = LATERAL / roll axis    (lean LEFT = positive, lean RIGHT = negative)
//     D3:D4 = LONGITUDINAL / pitch   (level ~+175; NOSE-DOWN tilt drops it to ~-110)
//     D5:D6 = VERTICAL axis          (~ -7770 at rest = -1 g)
//   SCALE ~7770 counts per g (from the resting vertical channel).
//   PROVEN by lean_3xl_3xr (bike rocked by hand on the sidestand, 3x left then 3x
//   right):
//     - D1:D2 swung +786..+1211 on the THREE left leans and -1024..-1525 on the
//       THREE right leans - signed and symmetric by direction. Clean 3L/3R pattern.
//     - D5:D6 magnitude SHRANK toward zero on every lean (-7770 -> -7617 at hardest),
//       exactly as gravity tilts off the vertical axis.
//     - VECTOR MAGNITUDE CONSERVED: sqrt(D1D2^2 + D3D4^2 + D5D6^2) held ~7770 across
//       all orientations = a constant 1 g gravity vector rotating between axes. At
//       the biggest right lean sqrt(1525^2 + 7617^2) = 7768 ~= rest 7770. That
//       conservation is the definitive accelerometer signature.
//   Implied lean angles were gentle hand-rocks: asin(1525/7770) ~= 11 deg right,
//   asin(1211/7770) ~= 9 deg left.
//   PITCH AXIS INDEPENDENTLY VALIDATED by a natural experiment (stand geometry):
//   ordering captures by odometer, D3:D4 held ~+175 (level) through EVERY front-wheel
//   test, then STEPPED to ~-110 exactly at the forklock capture - the moment the
//   front wheel came off the stand and the bike tilted nose-down onto the rear stand
//   only. Cleanest A/B: idle_94f (front stand ON) D3:D4=+175 vs idle_forward_tilt
//   (front stand removed) D3:D4=-112 = a 287-count step = asin(287/7770) ~= 2.1 deg
//   forward tilt, while D5:D6 (vertical) and D1:D2 (lateral) barely moved - a pure
//   fore-aft rotation, exactly as a pitch axis must behave. So ALL THREE axes are now
//   independently validated (lateral=lean test, vertical=gravity magnitude, pitch=
//   stand tilt). NOTE this means the "pitch NOT found on secondary" entry in the
//   speculation doc is also overturned - it was there all along in D3:D4.
//   *** OVERTURNS the speculation-doc "tilt/lean NOT on secondary" conclusion. The
//   IMU is a primary-bus module but its accel IS gatewayed here. The reason 0x122
//   never correlated with speed/power (which killed the battery-power idea) is that
//   an accelerometer reads GRAVITY at rest, not vehicle dynamics - the tell was the
//   near-constant -7770 vertical channel all along.
//   COMPANION FRAME: 0x126 is the matching 3-AXIS GYROSCOPE (CONFIRMED) - see its
//   block immediately below. Together 0x122 (accel) + 0x126 (gyro) form a full
//   6-AXIS IMU gatewayed onto secondary CAN.


// ---- 0x126 (294) : IMU 3-AXIS GYROSCOPE (angular rate) - CONFIRMED -----------
BO_ 294 IMU_GYRO_126: 8 IM
 SG_ gyro_roll_rate  : 7|16@0+ (1,-32768) [-32768|32767] "count" Vector__XXX
 SG_ gyro_pitch_rate : 23|16@0+ (1,-32768) [-32768|32767] "count" Vector__XXX
 SG_ gyro_yaw_rate   : 39|16@0+ (1,-32768) [-32768|32767] "count" Vector__XXX
// [CONFIRMED] 0x126 = 3-AXIS GYROSCOPE (angular RATE), same structure as the 0x122
//   accelerometer: three signed 16-bit pairs, offset-binary (value = raw - 32768):
//     D1:D2 = ROLL rate    (responds to SIDE-TO-SIDE shaking)
//     D3:D4 = PITCH rate   (responds to FORWARD-BACK shaking)
//     D5:D6 = YAW rate     (third axis; responded to both hand-shakes because manual
//                           input is never a pure single axis - treat yaw as [STRONG])
//   PROVEN by shakenbabysyndrome_sidetoside_forwardback_5xeach (bike shaken on the
//   stand, 5x side-to-side then 5x fore-aft):
//     - AXIS MATCH: D1:D2 (roll) oscillated hard in the SIDE-TO-SIDE burst and went
//       quiet in the fore-aft burst; D3:D4 (pitch) did the opposite - one-to-one with
//       the 0x122 accel roll/pitch axes.
//     - RATE-NOT-ANGLE (definitive): within the side-to-side burst, D1:D2 correlates
//       r=-0.68 with the DERIVATIVE of the 0x122 roll ANGLE, and only r=-0.05 with the
//       angle itself. Angular rate = d(angle)/dt, ~90 deg out of phase with angle -
//       exactly a gyro. Peak-to-peak (7826) exceeded the accel's (4362), as expected
//       for a rate driven by fast motion.
//   SCALE: raw counts; deg/s per count NOT pinned (needs a known rotation rate, e.g. a
//   turntable - not worth chasing for a display/telemetry feed).
//   HISTORY: 0x126 was long dismissed as noise / "0xFFFE not-available". The sentinel
//   just means that gyro axis is idle/unpopulated in some states; under motion all
//   three pairs come alive. With 0x122 (accel) this completes the IMU on secondary.


// ---- 0x128 (296) : PROPULSION / ABS STATUS (E2E, sparse ~0.2 Hz) -----------
BO_ 296 PROPULSION_ABS_128: 8 Vector__XXX
 SG_ front_brake_applied_128 : 47|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
// [CANDIDATE 2026-07-29 — "triangle-!" whole-suite WARNING-ICON fingerprint] Rider triggered the dash
//   warning icon on a real ride (s60) and rebooted to clear it (s61). An A/B (s60 warning vs s61
//   cleared-post-reboot + s59 normal, all controlled for riding) isolates a LATCHED ABS/traction
//   signature persisting until power-cycle, across THREE EHCU/motor frames:
//     0x128 D5 : 0x10 -> 0x70        (this frame's hard-decel/ABS-regen control block, heavily flagged)
//     0x161 D6 : 0x04/0x14 -> 0x74   (motor_status: extra 0x60 bits above the 0x10 limiter = DERATE)
//     0x3C8 D3 : 0x3F/0xDF -> 0xFF   (ABS status/validity word, all bits)
//     0x505 D1 : 0x00 -> 0x01        (latched power/boot flag)
//   All ABS/TC/limiter-class => matches the rider's "ABS/TC warning" read, and the motor-derate bit
//   implies it also LIMITS power (limp mode). RULES OUT the old 0x152 D2=0x0E lighting telltale (0x00
//   here). MODE CONFOUND REMOVED: the normal ride s59 was the SAME mode as s60 (0x44 = Eco/Range) yet
//   shows the NORMAL values, so the latch is warning-specific, NOT mode-driven. Remaining CAVEAT:
//   single occurrence, no onset, no live DTC captured. Confirm with the ONSET + a live DTC read while
//   the warning is present. See docs/livewire_s2_CAN_speculation.md.
// [CONFIRMED 2026-07-29 — 6-session review] D6 (front_brake_applied_128) = FRONT-BRAKE-APPLIED flag:
//   0x01 off / 0x02 on. Thresholded with hysteresis on the 0x324 front-brake pressure (sets ~200-270
//   raw, clears ~90-130). D6 vs 0x324 r = +0.81..0.91 across SIX sessions. DISCONFIRMED as rear/regen
//   by the s57 hard-regen event (tq=-260, rbrk=16, fbrk=0 -> D6 stayed 0x01). SUPERSEDES the frame-
//   catalog "0x128 D6 = 2-state status bit, unattributed." (EHCU/ABS = Bosch MSC; a front-pressure
//   threshold flag is native to that unit.)
//   D3/D4/D5 = [CANDIDATE] hard-decel / regen-control block - activate together ONLY during sustained
//   strong regen/hard braking (zero at standstill/cruise/accel; dissociated from the front-brake
//   flag: active with fbrk=309 in s28 AND fbrk=0 in s57, common factor tq~=-198 regen). D5 0x20 =
//   control-active bit; D3 = phase index {18,19}; D4 = 0-211 sawtooth (ABS/regen-blend modulation
//   output, NOT a clean magnitude). Single-event-per-session -> needs a graded/near-ABS braking
//   capture to settle (see the 0x128 census caveat + speculation doc). D7/D8 E2E.

// ---- 0x12A (298) : off-throttle / regen-active flag -------------------------
BO_ 298 STANDSTILL_FLAG_12A: 8 Vector__XXX
 SG_ standstill : 31|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
// [UPDATE 2026-07-27 — ride1 real-timestamp capture + deep review; double-verified.
//  RETRACTS "off_throttle_regen". 0x12A D4 = 0x40 is a debounced VEHICLE-STANDSTILL
//  flag (Bosch-style), NOT a regen indicator.]
//   Sets ~0.4 s after speed reads 0; clears ~0.34-0.56 s after sustained motion;
//   THROTTLE-INDEPENDENT (held through 22.5% launch throttle at 0 km/h). Transitions
//   ride the normal 200 ms grid.
//   REGEN MODEL KILLED BOTH WAYS: 0x00 through the ENTIRE 75mph passive-regen coast
//   and every ride1 regen phase; 0x40 held while throttle applied at standstill.
//   Corpus-wide: ZERO instances of 0x40 while moving (a hard invariant -> validate.py).
//   [REVERSE CORROBORATION 2026-07-30, ultracode] D4 is a standstill/drive-engaged flag, NOT a
//     direction bit: 0x00 in BOTH reverse-drive AND forward-drive, 0x40 only at idle/standstill
//     (reverse2x: 0x00 in 34 reverse-drive + 43 forward-drive rows, 0x40 in 124 idle rows). It
//     is the sole status byte that moves between regimes, and it tracks engagement not direction.
//   The old "0x40 during coast/regen" reading was standstill coincidentally co-occurring
//   with the end of those low-speed bench tests.
//   QUALIFIED: standstill is NECESSARY but not SUFFICIENT - a gating condition also
//   applies (candidates: dynamics-suite-valid, or 0x162 D4 state; ~5 s power-on
//   latency; 0x40 absent in gyro-0xFFFE rows). D4=0x80 is a THIRD state seen only in
//   mode-sweep captures, coincident with 0x134 entering/leaving 0x55/0x88/0x99 at
//   standstill (mode-hold). Both unresolved - see the speculation doc.
//   *** [RETRACTED 2026-07-29 — was "[NEW 2026-07-28] 0x12A D1 = a 2-LEVEL SPEED-BAND FLAG (0x40
//   rest/low, 0x80 above a speed threshold)"]: the speed-band read FAILS on full speed overlap -
//   s54 has 945-raw speed at 0x40 vs 237-raw at 0x80, so the two levels' speed distributions fully
//   OVERLAP. What actually happens: 0x12A D1 = a MOTION-GATED PARITY/ALTERNATION bit - it flips
//   0x40<->0x80 on essentially every consecutive MOVING frame (alternation 0.92/1.00/1.00/1.00 over
//   s28/s31/s44/s57) and is pinned to 0x40 at standstill. 0x80 is simply SUPPRESSED at standstill,
//   which is why its mean speed looked higher earlier (a gating artifact, not a speed band). Toggle
//   PASS (deterministic, 4 sessions); NOT a signal to wire. (Old speed-band means kept above for the
//   record: they were the standstill-suppression artifact, not a threshold.) ***


// ---- 0x133 (307) : see IGNITION_REAR_BRAKE_133 below (merged) ---------------



// ---- 0x134 (308) : RIDER SETTINGS status (mode + TC + related) ---------------
BO_ 308 RIDER_SETTINGS_134: 8 BCM
 SG_ ride_mode      : 7|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ mode_tc_status : 15|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ mode_config_d3 : 23|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ mode_config_d4 : 31|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
// [CONFIRMED] 0x134 D1 = ride-mode enum (high nibble = mode id):
//   0x22 Sport, 0x11 Street, 0x44 Eco, 0x33 Rain, 0x88 custom-A, 0x99 custom-B,
//   [NAMING 2026-07-29] "Street"/"Eco" were the rider's labels; per the OEM manual the factory modes
//   are Sport/Road/Range/Rain/Flat Track -> 0x11 Street = ROAD, 0x44 Eco = RANGE (Custom A/B are the
//   two app-programmable slots). All seven codes now confirmed via 3 mode-cycle captures.
//   0x55 = SEVENTH MODE (see below). Verified by cycling Sport->A->B->Rain->Eco->
//   Street->Sport and observing 0x134 D1 step 22->88->99->33->44->11->22 (clean
//   closure). 0x260 D1 mirrors.
// [CONFIRMED] 0x55 = FLAT TRACK MODE (the "hard lean" rider icon). Rider confirms
//   the leaning-rider mode IS Flat Track. It is reached by "activating" (hold Mode
//   in) SPORT: activating Sport does NOT keep id 0x22 with an overlay bit - it SWITCHES
//   the mode id to 0x55 (seen twice in modes_alltryactivated: 22 -> 55 -> 22 -> 55). So
//   Flat Track is Sport's activated variant, promoted to its own dedicated mode id.
//   It runs the Sport-tier power index (D3 low-nibble = 3, D4=0x30) with rear ABS off
//   (0x3C8 D4 bit7 set), its own default TC nibble (D2 = 0x54; low-nibble 4, distinct
//   from Sport's 3), and TC is still rider-toggleable to off (D2 = 0x59, low-nibble 9 -
//   confirmed by the modes_alltryactivated finale where the rider hand-disabled TC in
//   Flat Track: D2 went 0x54 -> 0x59). NOTE: this is NOT the "triangle-!" fault state
//   the rider once hit - Flat Track cuts REAR ABS ONLY and keeps TC available; the
//   fault dropped the WHOLE aid suite (TC + front & rear ABS). See 0x3C8 / fault notes.
// [CONFIRMED] THE "ACTIVATED" MODE VARIANT (hold the Mode button). Marked on the bus by
//   0x134 D3 HIGH NIBBLE 1 -> 4 (power-index low nibble UNCHANGED) and 0x134 D6 bit2
//   (0x04). Full sweep of activating all 7 modes (modes_alltryactivated) shows only
//   THREE modes have a functional activated variant, and each SWITCHES/overlays thus:
//     Sport (22) -> FLAT TRACK, id 0x55, D3=43, D6=04   (own mode id)
//     CustA (88) -> "Purple A",       D3=48, D6=04   (id stays 88, purple display)
//     CustB (99) -> "Purple B",       D3=49, D6=04   (id stays 99, bold/purple display)
//   Street/Rain/Eco: activating them produces NO change on secondary CAN at all (D3
//   high-nibble stays 1, D6 stays 0, rear ABS stays on) - matches rider's "only Sport
//   ->Flattrack and A/B->Purple were noticeable".
//   *** ACTIVATED vs REAR ABS OFF = SEPARATE axes, correlated only by CURRENT CONFIG. ***
//   Custom A/B are USER-PROGRAMMABLE from the LiveWire app, so what a mode's "activated"
//   variant DOES (rear ABS, TC, power) is itself configurable. The 100% co-occurrence we
//   see (every activated variant here also cuts rear ABS) therefore reflects how THIS
//   bike's A/B (and the factory Flat Track) are currently programmed - NOT an intrinsic
//   bus-level equivalence. Read the two signals as independent:
//     - 0x134 D6 bit2 / D3-hi=4  = "activated variant engaged" (generic state flag)
//     - 0x3C8 D4 bit7            = "rear ABS disabled" (a CONSEQUENCE that the mode's
//                                   programmed settings may or may not include)
//   The firmware keeps them as separate signals precisely because they are independently
//   configurable. DEFINITIVE DECOUPLE (now controllable, no fault needed): in the app,
//   program custom A's activated variant to KEEP rear ABS on, then capture - D6 bit2 will
//   set while 0x3C8 D4 bit7 stays 0. That single capture converts this from "correlated
//   under current config" to a clean independent proof. Until then: do NOT infer rear ABS
//   state from the activated flag or vice-versa; match each bit to its own frame.
// [CONFIRMED] 0x134 D2 = mode(high nibble) + status(low nibble). Low nibble
//   carries Traction Control state: within Sport, TC-on=0x23, TC-off=0x29
//   (i.e. low nibble 3=on, 9=off). Verified via idle TC-on->TC-off capture
//   (single toggle 0x23->0x29 at the switch press) AND independently the whole
//   75mph TC-off run read 0x134 D2 = 0x29 throughout.
//   CAUTION: D2 is a mode+status bitfield, not a pure TC bit. Match the low
//   nibble for TC, use D1 for mode. Other modes may set other low-nibble values
//   (Rain/Eco seen with different low nibbles) - treat unseen values as unknown.
// [CONFIRMED per-mode] 0x134 D3 and D4 are PER-MODE CONFIG bytes - each takes a
//   DETERMINISTIC value for every one of the 6 modes (cyclemodes capture):
//     mode    D1  D3  D4    0x260 D2
//     Sport   22  13  30    20
//     Street  11  11  10    10
//     Eco     44  1D  D0    40
//     Rain    33  2C  C0    30
//     CustA   88  18  80    80
//     CustB   99  19  90    90
//   ACTIVATED VARIANTS (hold Mode; D3 high-nibble=4, D6 bit2=1, rear ABS off):
//     FlatTrk 55  43  30    50   <- activated SPORT = Flat Track (own mode id 0x55)
//     PurpleA 88  48  80    80   <- activated CustA (id stays 88)
//     PurpleB 99  49  90    90   <- activated CustB (id stays 99)
//   (Street/Rain/Eco have NO functional activated variant on the bus.)
//   STRUCTURE: 0x134 D3 low-nibble == D4 high-nibble == a per-mode index
//   (3/1/D/C/8/9 for Sport/Street/Eco/Rain/CustA/CustB), and 0x260 D2 high-nibble
//   mirrors the mode id. So these carry the mode's SETTINGS bundle (regen level,
//   power map, throttle map). SEMANTIC split of the sub-fields is UNRESOLVED - would
//   need ground truth on each mode's actual regen/power settings to attribute which
//   nibble is which. For now: deterministic per-mode, usable to read the active mode
//   three independent ways (D1, D3/D4 index, 0x260 D2).


// ---- 0x15A (346) : FRONT brake lever + hazards ------------------------------
BO_ 346 FRONT_BRAKE_HAZARD_15A: 8 BCM
 SG_ front_brake : 47|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ front_brake_alt : 7|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ hazards     : 15|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
// [CONFIRMED] 0x15A D6 = FRONT brake lever: 0x00 released -> 0x40 pressed.
// [CONFIRMED] 0x15A D1 = SECOND front-brake indicator: 0x10 released -> 0x01
//   pressed. Perfectly correlated with D6 (224 frames at 0x01 while pressed,
//   6736 at 0x10 while released, zero disagreement) in the fast-spin + 3x front
//   brake capture. Either byte works; D1 is a cleaner 2-state read.
//   Isolated in brakelight_front_rear_passiveregen capture: active ONLY during
//   the front-brake segment, not rear, not regen. (0x15A D1 also moves front:
//   0x10->0x01.) 0x15A D2 remains hazards (0x00<->0x10) - same frame, diff byte.

// ---- 0x133 (307) : ignition + REAR brake ------------------------------------
BO_ 307 IGNITION_REAR_BRAKE_133: 8 BCM
 SG_ ignition_d1 : 7|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ rear_brake  : 31|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ wake_state  : 39|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
// [CONFIRMED 2026-07-28] 0x133 D5 = WAKE / ignition sub-status. 0x10 = awake/on in
//   EVERY powered state (idle E0, ride E0, charge 50), 0x20 = deep-off (only appears
//   in the ignition/boot transient alongside D1=0x20 OFF). Zero counterexamples across
//   the corpus; E2E CRC-clean. Distinct from D1 (system-state enum) - a coarser on/off.
// [CONFIRMED] 0x133 D4 = REAR brake lever: 0x00 released -> 0x10 pressed.
//   Isolated: active ONLY during the rear-brake segment (first time rear was
//   pressed in any capture). Front and rear are SEPARATE IDs - that's why the
//   earlier single-byte 0x136 guess failed.
//   ROBUSTNESS: rear LAMP was physically UNPLUGGED during this capture, yet
//   0x133 D4 still toggled cleanly => it is the LEVER SWITCH state, independent
//   of the bulb. No rear-bulb-out fault flag appeared on secondary in this
//   capture (a bulb-out fault, if any, may be on primary CAN or via UDS only).
// [CONFIRMED] 0x133 D1 = SYSTEM STATE enum (not just ignition on/off):
//     0x20 = OFF
//     0x60 = ignition ON, motor NOT enabled (accessory / stand-by)
//     0x80 = ENABLING (brief transitional state during START press)
//     0xE0 = MOTOR ENABLED / ready-to-drive
//     0x50 = CHARGING (AC charging in progress). CONFIRMED: appears in 2025 frames
//            of charge_1-1kw.csv and in NONE of the other 46 captures. The capture
//            also contains 0x60, i.e. it moves between charging and ignition-on.
//   Mapped with the full ign->enable->roll->brake->disable->off sequence capture.
//   (An earlier ignition-only capture never enabled the motor, so it only ever
//   showed 0x20/0x60 - hence the earlier incomplete "on/off" decode.)


// ---- 0x152 (338) : lighting + ignition bitfields ----------------------------
BO_ 338 LIGHTING_152: 8 BCM
 SG_ highbeam   : 23|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ ign_152_d2 : 15|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
// [STRONG] 0x152 D3 = high beam: 0x00<->0x04. Verified highbeam_on_2x capture.
//   D2 (byte 1) is a shared lighting/ignition bitfield (0x00/0x10/0xE0 at ignition) AND
//   carries a LATCHED WARNING TELLTALE at value 0x0E: 0x00 normal -> 0x0E warning, held ON
//   even at a standstill from ride session s15 onward (motion-INDEPENDENT, so NOT a headlight
//   beam), with NO stored DTC (rider ran diagnostics -> "no faults"). Rider attributes it to
//   an ABS/TC-related warning. [RIDE-CONFIRMED 2026-07-28; corrects the earlier "D2 = beam
//   bitfield" reading for the 0x0E value — that specific value is a warning telltale.]


// ---- 0x131 (305) : turn signal LAMP STATUS (live bulb on/off + side) --------
BO_ 305 TURN_LAMP_131: 8 BCM
 SG_ lamp_left  : 23|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ lamp_right : 31|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
// [CONFIRMED] 0x131 D3/D4 = LAMP STATUS (blinks at flash cadence = live bulb):
//   resting (off) = (D3=0x15, D4=0x50).
//   Left lamp lit : D3 0x15 -> 0x19   (blinks ~16 frames off / 17 on)
//   Right lamp lit: D4 0x50 -> 0x90   (blinks)
//   Hazards       : BOTH D3 and D4 blink (0x19 / 0x90)
//   This is the LAMP layer: D3/D4 oscillate ON<->OFF at the flash rate, so a
//   snapshot tells you whether that bulb is CURRENTLY lit. Use for a live blink
//   effect. Decode side: left uses D3, right uses D4.
//   Verified: left_signal_2x (only D3 blinks), right_signal_2x (only D4 blinks),
//   hazards_2x (both blink), idle (neither) captures.
// [REFINED 2026-07-29 — was "0x154 D4/D5 ... repeater artifact, do not use for turn state"]
//   0x154 D4/D5 is a STRUCTURED L/R TURN-SIGNAL REPEATER lane (promoted to BO_ 340 below), NOT
//   noise: every D4=0x10 aligns to 0x131 D3=0x19 (LEFT lit), every D4=0x01 aligns to 0x131 D4=0x90
//   (RIGHT lit), and D5=0x10 fires on the off-phase edges between D4 pulses. ~25 clean events across
//   s54+s57 with ZERO disagreement. 0x131 D3/D4 REMAINS the lamp source; 0x154 is a downstream echo
//   (usable as an L/R repeater, not as the primary turn state).

// ---- 0x154 (340) : TURN-SIGNAL REPEATER LANE (E2E) -------------------------
BO_ 340 TURN_REPEATER_154: 8 BCM
 SG_ turn_repeater_lr       : 31|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ turn_repeater_offphase : 39|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
// [STRONG 2026-07-29] Downstream repeater of the 0x131 turn lamps: D4 (turn_repeater_lr) 0x10 =
//   LEFT (aligns 0x131 D3=0x19), 0x01 = RIGHT (aligns 0x131 D4=0x90); D5 (turn_repeater_offphase)
//   0x10 fires on the off-phase edges between D4 pulses. ~25 clean events s54+s57, zero disagreement.
//   0x131 remains the lamp SOURCE - this is an echo lane. D1/D2 = [CANDIDATE] extra Slow-mode
//   indicator lanes (0x01/0x10, single session s57, not turn-driven; see speculation doc). D7/D8 E2E.

// ---- 0x3C4 (964) : UNKNOWN (contains rolling counters) ----------------------
BO_ 964 WALL_CLOCK_3C4: 8 BCM
 SG_ clock_hours   : 7|8@0+ (1,0) [0|23] "h" Vector__XXX
 SG_ clock_minutes : 15|8@0+ (1,0) [0|59] "min" Vector__XXX
 SG_ clock_seconds : 23|8@0+ (1,0) [0|59] "s" Vector__XXX
// [CONFIRMED 2026-07-28, frame-catalog + empirical verify] 0x3C4 D1:D2:D3 = REAL-TIME
//   CLOCK, hours:minutes:seconds. In newcap_4 (real timestamps) D3 (seconds) ticks +1/s
//   and wraps at 0x3B=59 exactly as D2 (minutes) increments; D1 = hours-of-day (max 0x17=23).
//   Clock advanced 116 s over 116 s of real time (ratio 1.003); 0 range violations. Free-
//   running through the ~8-min IM brownout (D2 38->46 across the gap) -> a wall clock, NOT
//   an uptime counter.
//   [REFINED 2026-07-30, ultracode round - cross-capture] 1:1 advance RE-CONFIRMED (s57
//   1502 clock-s over 1501.5 real-s, ratio 1.0003, monotonic). NOT civil-UTC-synced: the
//   clock-to-filename offset is a CONSTANT +6h38m across s57/s61/s60/s59/s28 (~10 s spread),
//   not the +7h that July PDT (UTC-7) would require -> a FREE-RUNNING clock with a fixed
//   offset (~22 min short of UTC), NOT GPS/civil-time-locked. Retracts the "GPS-synced" guess.
//   *** RESOLVES the old "0x3C4 D2 multi-purpose status byte" TODO: the "turn-intent"
//   0x0E/0x10/0x14 and the ABS-test 0x15/16/17 values were simply the MINUTES-of-recording
//   of those captures. RETRACTS notes.md's "No wall clock" claim. ***
//   D4=0x00, D5=0x30, D6=0x03 constant. Use 0x131 D3/D4 for turn state, not this.

