// ---- 0x184 (388) : VSC PROPULSION STATUS (E2E, ~2.5 Hz) --------------------
BO_ 388 PROPULSION_STATUS_184: 8 Vector__XXX
 SG_ drive_state_184     : 39|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ tc_intervention_184 : 47|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
// [STRONG] D5 (drive_state_184) speed-INVERSE (r=-0.80 vs rpm): 30 coast->20 moving->10 hard.
//   D6 (tc_intervention_184) flat 0xF0, steps F0->F1->F2 only in ride1 TC/slip = intervention
//   event indicator. D3/D4 = readiness bits (7D/90, 19/00). D7/D8 E2E. (Refines the old
//   "mostly-static; USB red-herring" note - the USB retraction stands, D5 is speed-linked.)
// [CORROBORATED 2026-07-28, s44 real timestamps] D6 fired 4 genuine TC micro-interventions
//   (F0->F1) on the hard launches: t=207.2 (thr 52%, td 542), t=333.8 (thr 80%, td 878,
//   rear-lead 44), t=335.7 (thr 34%, td 304), t=338.9 (thr 51%, td 516) - each lines up with a
//   >6% rear-wheel-lead episode (0x326) => real driven-wheel slip cut by an ACTIVE TC (TC ON,
//   rear ABS ON, no burnout, rear-lead max 8.5%). First TC micro-cuts captured on the streamed
//   corpus, confirming the D6 = TC-intervention read on true timing.
// [REFINED 2026-07-29 r1 — GRADED, not flat-0xF0] The identity (D6 = TC/slip intervention)
//   holds, but the "flat 0xF0 except discrete slip events" prose is WRONG. Under sustained fast
//   riding D6 is CONTINUOUSLY active across a graded band F0-FC with a DECAYING distribution
//   (s57: F0 27%, F1 43%, tapering off to FC) - it is a slip-intervention INTENSITY, not a
//   binary flag and not a uniform counter. The s44 discrete F0->F1 micro-cuts (each aligned to a
//   >6% rear-wheel-lead) remain valid as the low end of that same continuum.
// [CANDIDATE 2026-07-29 — pack-thermal / power-derate cluster] (comments only, not wired):
//   D1 = coarse pack-THERMAL / derate LEVEL index (range 25-30, ~6 levels; pinned 28 in
//   gentle/parked captures). In the hard s55 run (pack raw 81->101 = 41->61 degC) D1 correlates
//   r=+0.92/+0.93/+0.93 with the three 0x183 pack temps and -0.93 vs ambient.
//   *** DOWNGRADED to SPECULATIVE / UNRESOLVED 2026-07-29 r1 (adversarial QA - fails cross-session). ***
//   The single-ride s55 r=0.92 is a temp/SoC/time-COLLINEAR co-trend, and the cross-session
//   absolute levels are NON-MONOTONIC: D1 is pinned at EXACTLY 28 in 11/13 sessions spanning pack
//   temp 78-83 raw, yet s54 (pack 80-81 raw) reads 25-26 - BELOW the COOLER park sessions
//   (78-79 raw -> 28). If D1 rose with pack temp, the warmer s54 should read >= park's 28, not
//   less. This STRIKES the earlier "SURVIVES the disconfirmer: s54 stayed cool -> D1 low"
//   rationalization - s54 was NOT cool for the pack (80-81 raw) and still read low, which
//   refutes rather than confirms a temp/derate index. Purpose unresolved; do NOT wire.
//   D4 bit0 = readiness / power-NOT-limited flag: 0x19 (bit0=1) at light load -> 0x18 (bit0=0) under
//   heavy propulsion demand; clean split by drive_state_184 (D5) hi-nibble (0/1/2 light -> 9-15 hard).
//   D2/D3 = [SPECULATIVE] propulsion derate substate: D3 base 0x7D becomes a +1/frame rolling counter
//   in low-SoC/derate windows (refines the old "D3 = readiness bits 7D/90" - 0x90 was one counter
//   value); D2 hi-nibble = idle 0x50. Trigger unpinned - see speculation doc.

// ---- 0x186 (390) : HV ENERGY METER (E2E, ~1.8 Hz) -------------------------
BO_ 390 HV_ENERGY_186: 8 Vector__XXX
