// ROUND-4 PROMOTED FRAMES (2026-07-28) - previously undocumented IDs, now decoded
//   and CONFIRMED by cross-capture verification (each empirically re-checked). See
//   docs/livewire_s2_CAN_notes.md round-4 ledger for the full census context.
// ============================================================================

// ---- 0x137 (311) : IGNITION / AUTH PULSE -----------------------------------
BO_ 311 IGNITION_AUTH_137: 8 BCM
 SG_ auth_pulse : 7|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
// [CONFIRMED 2026-07-28] Appears ONLY in the startup/ignition captures (ignition,
//   startup_nofob, newcap_9); ABSENT from all ~59 idle/ride captures. D1 = a 3-value
//   pulse enum {0x00, 0x90, 0xA0} that interleaves with the 0x1C3/0x1C5 boot step
//   counter -> an ignition/keyless-auth handshake byte, not a running signal. Non-E2E.
//   (Kills the old "0x136/0x137 = brake" guess: front brake is 0x15A, rear is 0x133 D4.)

// ---- 0x164 (356) : BATTERY-ENERGY 4-PHASE MUX ------------------------------
BO_ 356 BATTERY_ENERGY_MUX_164: 8 Vector__XXX
 SG_ energy_mux_sel : 7|8@0+ (1,0) [0|96] "" Vector__XXX
// Structure fully documented in the 0x164 prose block above. energy_mux_sel = D1 phase
//   selector {0x00,0x20,0x40,0x60}; per-phase D2:D3 channel tag + D4:D5 value. E2E (D7/D8
//   = counter/CRC). ch(0x0331)==affine==ch(0x0382): one energy quantity in two scales.
// [UPDATE 2026-07-29] D2:D5 (gated on the D1 selector) = a WIDE coulomb-counted SoC/ENERGY register
//   in 3 scales (sel 0x20/0x40 positive ~676/1631 cts/%, sel 0x60 INVERTED DoD; direction-reverses
//   charge vs discharge, tracks SoC not voltage, 7 sessions); the "channel tags" are the register's
//   rolling high bytes. Units unpinned. Left as prose (not a wired SG_) because the value is
//   selector-gated - see the reframed 0x164 census block above; keep gating on D1 before any read.

