 SG_ boot_step_1c3 : 7|8@0+ (1,0) [0|13] "" Vector__XXX
BO_ 453 BOOT_STEP_1C5: 8 Vector__XXX
 SG_ boot_step_1c5 : 39|8@0+ (1,0) [0|13] "" Vector__XXX
// [CONFIRMED 2026-07-28] A synchronized power-up STEP COUNTER mirrored across two IDs:
//   0x1C3 D1 and 0x1C5 D5 both sweep 0x00..0x0D then wrap, with identical step values;
//   0x1C3 leads 0x1C5 by ~1-2 frames. Present ONLY in the 5 startup captures (3 independent
//   boots); absent from every idle/ride capture. A BCM<->partner boot handshake sequence,
//   non-E2E. (Promotes 0x1C5 out of "dark".)

// ---- 0x304 (772) / 0x320 (800) : EHCU/ABS INIT ANNOUNCEMENT (one-shot) -----
BO_ 772 ABS_INIT_304: 8 Vector__XXX
BO_ 800 ABS_INIT_320: 8 Vector__XXX
// [CONFIRMED 2026-07-28] A one-shot EHCU/ABS init-announcement PAIR, exactly ONE frame each,
//   ONLY in the ABS/brake-init captures (brakes_verification, tcabs_preinit); absent
//   everywhere else. Fixed payloads: 0x304 = [0C 18 00 00 0C 20 00 00], 0x320 = [0C 88 00
//   00 0C 90 00 00] - two mirrored half-words +0x08 apart. No variable field (constant
//   announcement), so no SG_. The 0x0C/18/20/88/90 constants' meaning is still open.

// ---- 0x395 (917) : TCU CLOUD-LINK / ACCOUNT-PAIRING STATUS -----------------
BO_ 917 TCU_PAIRING_395: 8 TCU
 SG_ pairing_status      : 7|24@0+ (1,0) [0|16777215] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ cellular_signal_395 : 47|8@0+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
// [STRONG - NEW 2026-07-28] pairing_status (D1:D3) = the TCU broadcasting whether the bike
//   is LINKED to a phone-app / cloud account. Captured the exact H-D app "Add Bike" pairing:
//   D1:D3 held 0x000000 for the first 31 s (through standby + kickstand) then flipped to
//   0xAFA9D0 at the instant the app reported SUCCESS, and stayed there. It is 0x000000 in
//   ALL 8 pre-pairing captures (idle/charge/ride/ignition, incl. ks-up+standby) across
//   different sessions - so no ordinary vehicle state produces it; it tracks ACCOUNT-LINK.
//   The pairing itself is OFF-BUS: no UDS/SecurityAccess on secondary, and the displayed
//   pairing code (e.g. 719517) appears in NO frame in any encoding - only this status flag
//   surfaces on the bus. *** OPEN: three candidate meanings, separable by two controlled
//   variables (power-cycle, app-open): (a) NVM "account-paired" flag - non-zero forever once
//   paired, survives restart with the app closed; (b) "cloud-link-active" - set whenever the
//   TCU has a live cellular link to the H-D backend; (c) "app actively connected" - set only
//   while the phone app is open and talking to the bike. [UPDATE 2026-07-28] SURVIVES A POWER
//   CYCLE: a post-reboot capture reads 0xAFA9D0 from its first frame. (c) is RULED OUT: the
//   value is identical with the app backgrounded, force-refreshed to the FOREGROUND, and after
//   reboot - app state does not affect it. The value is CONSTANT 0xAFA9D0 across ALL captures
//   (pairing / same-session / post-reboot / app-fg) = a status MARKER / stable identifier, NOT
//   a per-session token or a timestamp (0xAFA9D0=11512272 fits no time base and never changes).
//   It is NOT a CRC/hash of the VIN or ICCID (checked) -> derived from account/user data not
//   visible to us. CONFOUND on (a) vs (b): the TCU is a telematics module that stays alive
//   across a bike reboot (remote features), so its cloud link almost certainly never dropped -
//   "survives reboot" therefore does NOT separate a stored NVM flag from a persistent cloud
//   link. THE definitive test is UNPAIR the bike from the app: if 0x395 D1:D3 -> 0x000000 it is
//   confirmed the account-link status; a subsequent re-pair tells account-derived (same value)
//   vs per-pairing (new value). Leading read: a stable "account-linked" identifier.
//   *** [UPDATE 2026-07-29 — 10-session review] 0x395 D5:D6 = CELLULAR SIGNAL STRENGTH (supersedes
//   the old "slow accumulator-ish field" note AND the retracted 0x395 D5 rotation_latch above):
//   D6 (cellular_signal_395) = fine raw metric 59-199, higher=stronger; D5 hi-nibble = quantized
//   bars 2-6 derived from D6 (D6 mean per level 107/114/125/144; corr(D5hi,D6)=+0.83 global,
//   +0.92..0.95 within-ride). Discriminator: STATIONARY = signal-stable (park/charge D6 span 5-11,
//   D5hi pinned) vs MOVING = signal-volatile (city/freeway D6 span ~100, D5hi sweeps {2..6}) -
//   classic received-signal behaviour, uncorrelated with speed/power/SoC; broadcast ~0.05 Hz (~20 s
//   modem report cadence). [CANDIDATE/PLAUSIBLE] Ground truth = DT-II "TCU Signal Strength" data
//   item (+ a TCU 0x7D4 UDS signal DID); settle the bars=D5hi / higher=stronger polarity in the
//   garage by logging 0x395 while the dash bars change. Only D6 is wired; D5 hi-nibble = derived
//   bars (comment). ***

// ============================================================================
// UDS DIAGNOSTICS - CONFIRMED, observed live on secondary CAN
// ============================================================================
// The instrument cluster's own Diagnostics screen POLLS every module over UDS on
// this bus. Capturing that screen (diagnostics_listing.csv) gave confirmed module
// addresses because the responses matched the dash readout exactly.
//
// SERVICES OBSERVED IN USE BY THE DASH:
//   0x19 01 05   ReadDTCInformation / reportNumberOfDTCByStatusMask
//                response 0x59 01 <mask> <fmt> <countHi> <countLo>
//   0x22 F1EE    ReadDataByIdentifier - module ID / part number (ASCII, ISO-TP
//                multi-frame). This DID is CONFIRMED WORKING on this vehicle.
//
// ADDRESSING: standard UDS, response ID = request ID + 8.
//   Requests were sent to: 0x7E0, 0x7E2, 0x7E3, 0x7E4, 0x7E5, 0x7E6, 0x7E7,
//                          0x7D3, 0x7D4, 0x7F0, 0x790
//
// ============================================================================
// *** MODULE MAP - RESOLVED 2026-07-27c (active UDS sweep of all 9 modules) ***
//   Read this table; the derivation blocks below are the historical record of how
//   each address was pinned (kept for provenance, NOT open questions any more).
//     req / resp      module   basis
//     0x7E2 / 0x7EA   BCM      DTC_COUNT=3 == dash "BCM 3"; F191 41001171A
//     0x7E3 / 0x7EB   LHCM     DTC_COUNT=2 == dash "LHCM 2"; part 0819112-0010; VIN
//     0x7E4 / 0x7EC   VSC      F193 part 41001094A2 == H-D DT-II release notes; logs
//                              powertrain P-codes, monitors ABS+IMU. Double-locked.
//     0x7E5 / 0x7ED   RHCM     part 0812837-0010 / 813636-0066 adjacent to LHCM parts
//     0x7E6 / 0x7EE   RESS     per-cell voltage array on DIDs 0205/0210 (mV) - only
//                              the battery has that. F193 66000297.
//     0x7E7 / 0x7EF   EHCU     F1EE -> "40800178" == dash "EHCU 0 ID#40800178"
//     0x7D3 / 0x7DB   OBC/HV   4-ch sensor cluster 0200/0210; lifetime counter FEE0;
//                              F193 41001111A5 (shares VSC's 41001 HV-supplier family)
//     0x7D4 / 0x7DC   TCU      TELEMATICS - eSIM ICCID (0298), LIVE GPS position (0200,
//                              2x float32 lat/lon; multi-session track across the 2026-07-28
//                              burst, NOT a stored fix), LIVE serving PLMN (0296, DYNAMIC:
//                              Verizon <home-PLMN-redacted> @ s6 -> T-Mobile 310/260 across the burst, two
//                              searching->register transitions). CONFIRMED - see uds_data_map.md.
//     0x7F0 / 0x7F8   ID-only  identification-only ECU: F1E8/F1EB.. IDs, NO data
//                              (FDxx/FExx) blocks. Not the TCU; purpose = ID responder.
//   SILENT (no module): 0x790, 0x7E0 (and bench guesses 0x7E1,0x7D0,0x7D1,0x7D2).
//   IMU is NOT a UDS responder - it has no diagnostic address; it is monitored by
//   the VSC (0x7E4), which logs its lost-comms DTCs. Do not look for a 0x7Ex IMU.
//   *** [OEM MANUAL CROSS-CHECK 2026-07-29 — HD Electrical Diagnostic Manual via DT-II HD-48650] ***
//   The factory manual is organised by FUNCTION, not by ECU, and NEVER exposes UDS addresses/SIDs/
//   DIDs (it's a DT-II tool manual) - so it does not contradict this address map; the addresses are
//   OUR discovery. Its module-ownership rule DOES refine the roster:
//     - VSC is NOT a separate module - it is the SUPERVISORY FUNCTION of the PEU ("PEU/VSC"). 0x7E4
//       is that unit's secondary-bus face; the PEU/inverter (primary bus) is the SAME physical ECU.
//     - OBC stores no own DTCs -> codes appear as "PEU/OBC" (matches 0x7D3 above).
//     - LHCM / RHCM / IMU store NO DTCs (they answer UDS ID but hold no fault memory) - confirms the
//       IMU note above and the switch-pod nature of LHCM/RHCM.
//     - DTC-STORING modules per the manual: ABS(EHCU), BCM, IM, PEU/VSC, RESS, TCU.
//   The manual's U-code routing table independently CONFIRMS this inventory from the OEM side:
//     U0121->EHCU, U0125->IMU, U0156->IM, U0140->BCM, U0141->LHCM, U0142->RHCM, U0198->TCU,
//     U019B->PEU/OBC, U01A1-5->RESS, U0293->PEU/VSC. Codes are 7-char (5 base + 2 Failure-Type Byte).
//   Full DTC catalogue + FTB decode + routing table: docs/livewire_s2_DTC_reference.md.
//   *** [ROUND-4 2026-07-28] "9 modules" is a FLOOR, not a ceiling. ***
//   A 10th diagnostic responder exists: ID 0x6E6 is NOT a periodic frame but an ISO-TP/
//   UDS RESPONSE channel (carries 59 02 ReadDTC, multi-frame 62 F1 80/81/93 ReadDID, and
//   7F NRCs) whose REQUEST id 0x6DE never appears on secondary -> a gatewayed/internal H-D
//   diagnostic address OUTSIDE the mapped nine. Also 0x7F2 is a UDS request to a further
//   unmapped module. So the map is "9 mapped + >=1 more (req 0x6DE / resp 0x6E6) + 0x7F2".
//   [LIVE 2026-07-28] Actively sending 0x22/0x19 to 0x6DE and 0x7F2 gets NO response - they
//   are PASSIVE-only (an internal module-to-module diagnostic exchange we overhear, not one
//   we can elicit from the DLC tap). So 0x6E6 is real but not reachable by us actively.
