//   DEFINITIVE METHOD (tap can TX): read F18C/F187 from each address and/or
//      match the dash Diagnostics ID# list to the captured serials. See below.
//   NOTE: dash DISPLAY ORDER does NOT equal poll order. The tester sends requests
//   in ascending CAN-ID (arbitration) order - verified: the 0x22 round went
//   0x790,7D3,7D4,7E0,7E2,7E3,7E4,7E5,7E6,7E7,7F0 = strictly ascending. And the
//   known modules break display order anyway (display: BCM 2nd, EHCU 3rd, LHCM
//   5th; by address: BCM 0x7E2, LHCM 0x7E3, EHCU 0x7E7). So ordering cannot be
//   used to map the remaining six.
//
// DID SUPPORT MATRIX (important):
//   0x22 F1EE is supported ONLY by the EHCU (0x7EF). Every other module answers
//   0x7F 22 31 = NRC 0x31 requestOutOfRange. So F1EE is not a universal ID DID on
//   this vehicle - other modules need different DIDs (try F190 VIN, F187 part
//
// *** WHY THERE IS UDS TRAFFIC DURING NORMAL OPERATION ***
//   It is NOT tied to diagnostics or to the keyless code start. Identification-DID
//   polling appears in most captures - 39 in a normal boot, 71 in the ABS self-test
//   capture, 34 in the tyre-pressure capture, 30 in the no-fob code start - and
//   recurs in BURSTS during a long run (at ~17 % and ~91 % of a 5-minute capture).
//   MOST LIKELY PURPOSE: module inventory for OTA UPDATES. The S2 is LiveWire's
//   first bike with over-the-air updates, and the TCU needs each module's part and
//   software numbers to decide what updates apply. F18C/F191/F193/F1EC/F1FB are
//   exactly the DIDs for that.
//
// *** DID LIST HARVESTED FROM THE BIKE'S OWN TRAFFIC (better than blind scanning) ***
//   The bike also polls NON-identification DIDs. These are live-data candidates and
//   are known-good because the vehicle itself requests them:
//     0x7EE : 0x0256, 0x025A, 0x025B, 0x025C, 0x025E, 0x025F, 0x0263, 0x0264,
//             0x0269, 0x0270, 0x020E     <- a whole 0x02xx family, i.e. this module
//                                           is being read for a live data block
//     0x7EA (BCM)  : 0x1001            -> 33 09 97
//     0x7EC        : 0x0205            -> 00 48 24
//     0x7EF (EHCU) : 0x0151            -> ASCII 'RGC'
//   START ANY UDS EXPLORATION HERE rather than scanning blindly - these are DIDs the
//   vehicle demonstrably supports.
//
//
// *** MODULE IDENTIFICATION DATA CAPTURED (startup_nofob_codestart_13131) ***
//   During a no-fob / code-entry startup the IM polled identification DIDs from all
//   modules. THE OTHER MODULES DO NOT SUPPORT F1EE - they answer F18C, F191, F193,
//   F1EC, F1FB (0x7F8 uses F1E8/F1EB/F1EC/F1ED). That is exactly why the earlier
//   F1EE-only scan returned nothing but the EHCU.
//   CAPTURED IDs:
//     0x7DB (req 0x7D3): F18C serial '<serial-redacted>'  F193 supplier '41001111A5'
//     0x7EB (req 0x7E3): F1EC '0819112-0010'  F1FB '813635-0044'      = LHCM
//     0x7EC (req 0x7E4): F18C serial '<serial-redacted>'  F193 '41001094A2'
//     0x7ED (req 0x7E5): F1EC '0812837-0010'  F1FB '813636-0066'
//                        F18C '<serial-redacted>'  F191 hardware '71500541541'
//     0x7EE (req 0x7E6): F18C serial '<serial-redacted>'  F193 supplier '66000297'
//     0x7F8 (req 0x7F0): F1E8 '32700101'  F1EB '170'  F1EC '130'  F1ED '340'
//   INFERENCE: 0x7ED is very likely the RHCM. Its part numbers (0812837-0010 /
//   813636-0066) share the exact FORMAT and ADJACENT NUMBERING with the CONFIRMED
//   LHCM at 0x7EB (0819112-0010 / 813635-0044) - left and right hand control
//   modules would be sequential parts from one supplier.
//   0x7DB and 0x7EC share a supplier-code format (41001111A5 / 41001094A2), so they
//   are probably a related pair from one vendor.
//   TO FINISH THE MAP: read these DIDs with the dash Diagnostics page open and match
//   each returned ID against the on-screen module list.
//
//   number, F189 software version, F18C serial).
//   EHCU also emits NRC 0x78 (responsePending) before its real answer - a normal
//   "wait, working on it" and a sign it does real work for the request.
//
// OBSERVED CHANGE BETWEEN CAPTURES: LHCM DTC count went 2 -> 3 between the two
//   diagnostics captures. Something logged a new fault in between (plausibly all
//   the wheel-spinning / ABS self-test activity). Useful: DTC counts are live.
//
// ============================================================================
// DECODING FULL DTCs (fault codes) FROM A PASSIVE CAPTURE
// ============================================================================
//   Beyond DTC *counts* (0x19 01), the bike also runs the FULL read - service
//   0x19 sub 0x02 (reportDTCByStatusMask) - and we can decode the actual codes
//   from a capture WITHOUT sending anything. Proven on faulted_IMoff_restarted.csv.
//   Tooling: `python3 validate.py --dtc CAPTURE.csv`.
//
//   REQUEST : <req_addr>  03 19 02 <statusMask>     (mask 0x09 = confirmed|failing)
//   RESPONSE: <req+8>      59 02 <availMask> then N x 4-byte records, ISO-TP framed:
//     ISO-TP PCI on byte D1:  0x_0 single-frame (len=low nibble),
//                             0x1_ first-frame (len=(nibble<<8)|D2),
//                             0x2_ consecutive-frame (seq=low nibble).
//     Each 4-byte record = [b0 b1]=DTC, [b2]=failure-type byte, [b3]=statusOfDTC.
//       letter = top 2 bits of b0: 00=P 01=C 10=B 11=U ; code = low14 bits as 4 hex.
//       status bits (ISO14229): 0x08 confirmed, 0x20 failedSinceClear,
//                               0x80 warningIndicatorRequested (lit a lamp), 0x01 failing now.
//     Negative resp 0x7F 19 78 = responsePending (module busy/booting - normal).
//
//   *** ONLY these SAE-standard codes are confident; the rest are LiveWire-proprietary
//   (target inferred from SAE norms, may be reassigned): ***
//     U0001 High-Speed CAN Bus | U0121 Lost Comm ABS Module | U0125 Lost Comm
//     Multi-axis Accel Sensor (=our 6-axis IMU) | U0155/U0156 Lost Comm Instrument
//     Cluster/Info-Center (=the IM) | P0560 System Voltage.
//
//   FAULT EVENT DECODED (faulted_IMoff_restarted, rider tripped it via RH controls;
//   IM went dark, bus stayed alive, hand-restarted). The scan's fingerprint:
//     - U0156 logged by 4 modules (BCM, LHCM, EHCU, VSC) = everyone lost THE IM.
//     - VSC also logged U0121 (lost ABS) + U0125 (lost IMU) + P0560 System Voltage.
//     - U0001 CAN-bus fault. => a brief POWER/VOLTAGE brownout dropped nodes off the
//       live bus. NOT an idle timeout (a timeout stores nothing and triggers no scan).
//     - EHCU C1021 carried status 0x88 (warningIndicatorRequested) - a lamp-lighting
//       chassis fault, a plausible source of a dash warning triangle.
//
// *** MODULE MAP EXTENDED: 0x7E4/0x7EC = VSC (Vehicle Supervisory Controller). ***
//   Three-way convergence: (1) its F193 part number '41001094A2' (line above) matches
//   the VSC part (41001094A2D) in the H-D Digital Technician II release notes; (2) in
//   the fault scan 0x7E4 is the module logging POWERTRAIN P-codes (P0560/P1100); (3) it
//   is the module that monitors ABS + IMU comms (U0121/U0125) - exactly a supervisory
//   controller's scope. So of the six unmapped modules, VSC = 0x7E4/0x7EC is now solid.
//   (Digital Technician II is H-D's dealer tool - it DOES support the S2DM: authenticated
//   DTC read/clear with official code text, live-data PID lists, actuator tests, and
//   reflash. It has the OEM DTC-description table we lack - the thing that would name the
//   proprietary U1xxx/C1xxx/B-codes above. Our edge: passive, real-time full signal map
//   + we just read these DTCs with NO tool and NO authentication.)
//
// IMPLICATION FOR BMS/MOTOR DATA: UDS is live and working from the DLC, the
//   gateway relays it, and 0x22 is accepted. Reading RESS/PEU data that is NOT
//   broadcast on secondary is therefore a matter of finding the right DIDs at the
//   right address - the transport is proven. Keep to 0x22 reads on a stand.
//
// ============================================================================
// UDS-DERIVED CALIBRATION / CROSS-CHECKS (2026-07-27c, active reads on a stand)
// ============================================================================
//   Newly readable UDS ground truth was used to pin scales the broadcast bus lacked:
//   - TORQUE ZERO-POINT + LIVE TORQUE: VSC (0x7E4) DID 0207 returned a torque/command
//     value that brackets the 0x161 zero anchor - consistent with torque_request/delivered
//     = word minus 5000 (the 5000 offset now has a second, independent witness).
//     [EXPANDED 2026-07-28, moving rides] words @4/@6/@8 (offset 5000) = LIVE applied/
//     requested/delivered torque, CONFIRMED under load on s28 (r=1.0) and s31 (@8 r=0.999,
//     @4 r=0.992). word0 = 0x1ADB = 6875 = +1875 drive clamp; word1 = 0x0EA6 = 3750 = -1250
//     regen clamp (constant defaults). The +/- clamp magnitudes are UNTESTED / NEVER REACHED
//     across the whole s25-s37 burst (peak applied +825 = 44% of +1875 on s28's hardest
//     launch; s31 26%; charge sessions <=2%) - so +/-1875 / -1250 remain UNPROVEN inference,
//     not measured limits. word1 was seen to dynamically tighten -1250 -> -230 under load in
//     s28 ONLY (candidate; s31/s32/s34/s35 held it at the -1250 default).
//   - ROAD SPEED (LIVE, new 2026-07-28): VSC (0x7E4) DID 020C word0 (u16@0, offset 0x8000)
//     = LIVE signed road speed; byte2 = drive-state (0x01 stop / 0x02 move). CONFIRMED r=1.0
//     vs broadcast speed on moving s28/s31; pinned at 0x8000/byte2=01 at standstill across
//     all stationary sessions (s25/s26/s27/s29/s32-s35). (020C was previously ABSENT from
//     the DBC entirely.)
//   - PACK CURRENT (corrected 2026-07-28): RESS (0x7E6) DID 0209 word0 (u16@0) = PACK
//     CURRENT, ~0.26 A/count, offset 1562 counts at 0 A (fit 1562 + 3.84*I); holds
//     OPPOSITE-SIGN across s28 discharge (n=7) and s32/s33/s34/s35 charge - a constant
//     cannot do that. u16@3 (b3:b4) = the 2nd HV current-sense channel "B" (see the CHANNEL-B
//     note just below - it was formerly guessed "instantaneous vs averaged"). 0209 is
//     NOT a pack-voltage reference; the earlier "0209 = pack voltage" reading is dead (an
//     idle-trap concatenation - see the CORRECTION in the CELL_VOLTAGE_182 block, ~L1733).
//     [FULL-ENVELOPE CONFIRM 2026-07-29] The high-rate streamed rides sampled the deep-
//     discharge regime the slow polls missed: word0 = 1562 + 3.888*I, r=0.996, over I -240..+35 A
//     (s54 to -123 A, s55 to -239 A, s57 to -240 A), slope 3.888 identical s55/s57. AIRTIGHT
//     across the full current envelope - the pack-current attribution is now decisive.
//     [CHANNEL-B CONFIRMED 2026-07-29 r1] RESS 0209 u16@3 (b3:b4) = the SECOND HV current-sense
//     channel "B" (OEM prior: two HV current channels A/B, correlation-checked P0B1300 A/B).
//     It is a NARROW-RANGE, HIGH-PRECISION channel with the SAME encoding as word0/channel A
//     (~1562 + 3.888*I): it tracks the wide-range word0 to within ~1-4 counts at steady state
//     (rock-steady +2-count offset in the |I| < ~33 A band) and HARD-SATURATES at raw ~1432
//     (about -33 A) - it clamps to a constant while word0 keeps falling (min word0 = 624 at
//     I = -241 A, s55/s57), so at the WOT-transient extreme word0 reads -58 A while b3:b4 pins
//     at -33 A. A moving-average copy would LAG smoothly there, not CLIP to a constant - so this
//     is a distinct range-limited sensor, not a filtered copy. 0209 is a clean 6-byte
//     SINGLE-FRAME DID (no ISO-TP splice risk), so the reading is splice-immune. Evidence: s55
//     idle 061a/0618, s55 05da/05d7 (-16.5/-17.2 A), 05c5/05c1 (-21.9/-22.9 A); r(word0,pack_i)
//     +0.996/+0.997/+0.993 (s55/s54/s57).
//   - HV 0235 byte5 = COARSE PACK TERMINAL-VOLTAGE byte (~2.55 V/count, b5 ~= 0.39*pack_v).
//     HV/OBC box (0x7D3) DID 0235, byte5. *** DOWNGRADE / RE-ATTRIBUTION 2026-07-29 r1
//     (adversarial QA): this was PROMOTED 2026-07-29 as a "coarse pack/module-CURRENT mirror"
//     (b5 ~= 142 + 0.20*I, r=0.94 s55 / 0.91 s57) - that label was a LOAD-SAG-TRAP ARTIFACT and
//     is RETRACTED. Under load, terminal V and current move together, so a voltage byte fakes a
//     current correlation. The discriminator is fitting b5 against BOTH and comparing
//     slope-stability: pooled over s28+s44+s54+s55+s57 (n=62) r(b5,pack_v)=+0.999 vs
//     r(b5,pack_i)=+0.850 - voltage wins decisively, AND the voltage-model slope is SESSION-STABLE
//     (0.34-0.45 ct/V) while the current-model slope WANDERS 3x (0.065->0.218 ct/A), the signature
//     of a true line vs a coincidence. So b5 = a coarse pack TERMINAL-VOLTAGE byte, NOT current.
//     (The genuine coarse/fine current channels are RESS 0209 word0/channel-B above; 0235 b3:b4
//     is the separate DC-link voltage node.) *** [METHODOLOGY: before labeling a byte "current",
//     also fit it vs voltage/SoC and require the winning model's slope to be session-stable.] ***
//   - PACK-VOLTAGE REFERENCE: RESS (0x7E6) DID 021F (~1 V/count) matched broadcast pack_v
//     to +/-1 V across s25/s26/s28/s29/s31/s32/s33/s34/s35 (range 365-395 V, discharge +
//     charge), plus VSC (0x7E4) DID 0220 - THESE, not 0209, confirm the 0x181/0x163 pack-V
//     scale (0.0625 V/count on 0x163, 1 V/count on 0x181) against a BMS-internal value.
//   - STATE OF CHARGE (corrected 2026-07-28): RESS DID 0213 = ~88.3% is INTERNAL FINE
//     SoC/SoE in 0.01% - it RISES on charge (8825->8869), so it is NOT SoH (SoH cannot
//     rise intra-session). The SoH-like reference is RESS DID 020E (pinned ~97% while real
//     display-SoC was ~83%). The 0x227x fine-SoC value is replicated across >=6 DIDs. The
//     broadcast display-SoC is on 0x185; a slow secondary byte matching 0213 is not pinned.
//     [STREAMED-RIDE CONFIRM 2026-07-28] 0213 is now confirmed LOAD-RESPONSIVE: it dips on
//     discharge (s28 r=0.97 vs pack_i n=19; s31 r=0.99) and rises on charge (s32/s33/s34/
//     s35) => voltage-instantaneous INTERNAL SoC%, sitting ~18-22 pts ABOVE the broadcast
//     display-SoC 0x185 (s25: 87.2% vs 69%). Reinforces "NOT display SoC, NOT SoH."
//   - CELL ARRAY: RESS DIDs 0205 / 0210 return the per-cell mV list - the same quantity 0x182
//     broadcasts as min/max/avg. The mapper's copy is TRUNCATED at its 46-byte hex cap (23 of
//     ~96 cells; 3997-4005 mV pre-charge), and 0205 was never in a STREAMED poll list, so the
//     full array is NOT yet captured. The stream path DOES reassemble full ISO-TP untruncated
//     (proven: RESS 025E returned 99 words, 0256 100 words), so one full 0205 read = every cell
//     voltage + a direct series COUNT. DONE (s25): full 0205 = 96 words = 96 CELLS (avg 3879 mV,
//     spread 5 mV, sum 372.4 V; cells are DIRECTION-RESPONSIVE - sag on discharge s28/s31,
//     rise on charge s32-s35). [CORRECTED 2026-07-28: the "0209 stayed 400.106 = rated-max
//     96x4.168 -> confirmed constant" clause that stood here was WRONG - 0209 word0 is PACK
//     CURRENT, not a rated-max constant; the 400.106 was an idle-trap concatenation. See the
//     CORRECTION at ~L1733-1738.] SERIES COUNT PINNED 96S (see the CELL_VOLTAGE_182 block).
//   - EHCU ABS BLOCKS RESOLVED 2026-07-28 (streamed moving rides s28/s31, real timestamps):
//     020F (4 B) = DUAL PER-WHEEL SPEED, u16@0 = FRONT, u16@2 = REAR, 0/0 at standstill,
//     r=1.000 vs broadcast 0x326 wheel_speed_front/rear; scale ~25x the 0x326 raw count
//     (~250 counts/km/h, ~0.004 km/h/count); REAR only ever LEADS FRONT (+256 quanta, ~2-4%
//     under power = mild TC-active slip; NO burnout captured). 0212 (8 B) u16@4 = FRONT-BRAKE
//     PRESSURE, r=1.0/0.999 vs broadcast front-brake (0x15A) on s28/s31 (range 0->415). [SCALE
//     REFINED s44 2026-07-28: NOT 1:1 - broadcast ~= 1.214*0212 + 14, i.e. 0212 ~= 0.79x
//     broadcast, r=0.999 over the wide 0->2241 range; same physical quantity, two scaled
//     encodings - the prior s22/s28 "identity" is refined to a 0.79 scale factor. 0212's slow
//     poll capped at 1461 ct, missing the 2241 broadcast peak.] Other words const 0; byte5/6
//     low nibble steps 0/2/4/6 = candidate parked brake-lever position/state; absolute pressure
//     scale still open (no bar/psi reference). 0210 (5 B) byte1 = BRAKE-ACTIVE flag (0->1 on a
//     press, s29), 0 on zero-brake. 0200/0211 = 12 V aux rail (~14 V, 0xAE=174), NOT a wake/
//     ignition counter. CANDIDATE validate.py oracle: EHCU 020F u16@0/@2 / 25 ~= broadcast
//     0x326 front/rear (s28/s31 now log UDS + broadcast simultaneously). CAVEAT: EHCU 021B
//     (ABS op/event counters) returned NRC/no-response to the streamed 191-DID poll in s26 -
//     its decode rests on the single earlier active-sweep read only.
//   - THROTTLE / TWIST-GRIP (CONFIRMED 2026-07-28, cross-session s28+s44): VSC (0x7E4) DID
//     0205 byte0 = LIVE throttle / twist-grip position, b0 ~= 2.7x throttle% (2.55x s28 /
//     2.64-2.75x s44), ZERO-ANCHORED (b0=0 whenever throttle=0; 2 anchors s44). Distinct field
//     within the VSC 0205 per-channel array (NOT the RESS 0205 cell array - a different module).
//     s44 moving throttle sweep: r=1.000, n=6 => promoted from candidate. Raw grip counts are
//     NOT on secondary CAN (nearest broadcast is 0x161 throttle%).
//   - LONGITUDINAL ACCEL / TRACTION-DEMAND (CONFIRMED 2026-07-28 w/ caveat, s28+s44): BCM
//     (0x7E2) DID 0202 byte8 = longitudinal accel / net drive-demand; s28 r=0.93 vs long_g
//     (n=413); s44 r(b8,acc_lon)=0.931, r(b8,torque_del)=0.943 (n=256). Byte oscillates ~78-129,
//     rest-anchor ~106 (=0 g) on charge (r~=0 vs pack current => rules out battery/thermal).
//     CAVEAT: accel and drive-torque are COLLINEAR on a bike, so accel-vs-demand is not fully
//     separable (b8 fits the smooth underlying axis better than the noisy raw acc_lon). Distinct
//     from the replicated 4/3/1/3/1 ADC-group words in the same DID.
//   - CHARGER / OBC BOX 0x7D3 RESOLVED 2026-07-28 (the s32-s48 external charge run first woke
//     these DIDs - they are dark except during AC charge): DID 0232 = CHARGER/PLUG-STATE word,
//     00 00 02 00 whenever NOT taking charge (parked s27, riding s28/s31, AND the mid-charge
//     UNPLUGGED ride s44) vs 02 01 02 02 for the entire duration of charging (s32/s39/s48) -
//     100% separation over 12 sessions; the identical field is mirrored at HV 0200 bytes 8-11.
//     DID 0209 = FF + charge-current byte (byte1 = 0x00 not-charging / 0x4F=79 at CC ~11 A /
//     0x24=36 at CV taper ~4 A); FE10 and FEE1 carry the SAME body (FE10 = FF-prefix, FEE1 =
//     00-prefix) with a trailing 16-bit charge-magnitude word (0xB710 @~11 A -> 0x6B62 @~4 A);
//     zero-at-not-charging + A/B (s44 unplugged = 0) => charge-current/charge-power indicator,
//     absolute A-scale open. This REFRAMES the prior "FE10/FEE1 not a coulomb accumulator"
//     refutation - they ARE a live charge-current register. DID 0201 word@4 (+ the 0200 ~700
//     sensor triplet) = charge-gated CHARGER/OBC TEMP: a thermal ARC ~714-754 (idle/unplugged)
//     -> 885-928 (CC peak) -> COOLS to 821 as CV current tapers (a temp cools when current
//     drops; a voltage/SoC would not) - promotes the "internal sensor cluster, scale suspect";
//     x0.1C-minus-offset scale still open. DID FEE0 is CHARGE-STATE-MULTIPLEXED (~4333 not-
//     charging / ~1520 charging, non-monotonic WITHIN a charge session) - this RETRACTS the
//     "FEE0 = monotonic lifetime op counter" reading and reconciles the doc's own contradiction
//     (the "decrements to ~1523" was the CHARGE state; "increments 4335->4337" was idle - both
//     real, different states). Meaning (time/energy estimate?) still open.
//   - RESS ACCUMULATORS ARE SIGN-BINNED 2026-07-28 (charge run vs s28/s44 discharge rides):
//     025A/025B (20x BE32) split charge vs discharge into SEPARATE dwords - dword@32 (idx8) =
//     cumulative CHARGE-Ah (advances ONLY on charge: s32/s39/s48; FROZEN on discharge rides),
//     while dword@12 (idx3) + dword@72 (idx18) = cumulative DISCHARGE-Ah (advance ONLY on
//     discharge: s28 +10/+37 ct, s44 +11/+43 ct; FROZEN on charge). Mutually-exclusive freezing
//     => not a lone co-trend. This refines the earlier "only idx8 ticks" (that was the charge
//     bucket). A SECOND, distinct accumulator axis: 025C/0269/0270 (120 B = 30x BE32, 4x5
//     zero-delimited buckets) bin by SoC BAND and are SIGN-INDEPENDENT - dword@84 (idx21, lower-
//     SoC bucket) advances on the s28/s31 rides then freezes; dword@88 (idx22, ~90% bucket)
//     advances in BOTH s44 discharge AND s48 charge, with the active bucket handing off idx21->
//     idx22 as SoC crosses ~88-89%. Per-count scale CANDIDATE (small deltas; 120-B DIDs are also
//     ISO-TP-cross-stitch-prone - validated here against clean headers only).
//   - RESS 020D IS A MIN/AVG/MAX ROLLUP, not 9 per-module values (resolves the map's open
//     "per-module min-cell vs temp"): b0=b1=b2=b5=b8 are ALWAYS bit-identical (8/8 sessions) =
//     a repeated coulomb/display-SoC scalar (~1%/ct) that rises 61->95 over the charge and
//     tracks broadcast 0x185 display-SoC (distinct from 0213's voltage-instantaneous fine SoC,
//     which saturates near the top) - this RESOLVES the s28 "0213 87% vs display 67%" gap: 020D
//     is the wide-range coulomb-SoC source, 0213 is voltage-instantaneous. b4 = the 0206 per-
//     cell-metric ARRAY MEAN (matches round(mean(0206)) in 6/8 clean reads), b3/b7 ~= min, b6 ~=
//     max; CAVEAT 2/8 reads (s27,s44) return an anomalous variant (b4=15) = a multiplex/poll
//     artifact, so the min/avg/max mapping is PLAUSIBLE not airtight.
//   - RESS 020C = FF-window LOW BYTE of 0209 word0 (PACK CURRENT), value-exact on aligned
//     samples (s27 ff1a, s44 ff b6 = 0209 0x05B6 discharge excursion, s48 ff2a) - CORRECTS the
//     low-hanging audit's "020C -> 0209 pack-V (mid byte)" fold-in (0209 is current, not V).
//   - VSC 0220 (refined 2026-07-28 over the full charge span): u16@4 = pack TERMINAL V, pinned
//     ~1 V/count across 361 V (s28 discharge sag) -> 402 V (full charge), matching broadcast
//     pack_v within +/-1-2 V - upgrades the prior single "~386 V" point. b0b1 (u16@0) is a
//     SEPARATE near-constant NOMINAL/rated ~392-396 V field (the "0x0189 setpoint" the doc had
//     dropped is real, just not the terminal node). b2=0x64=100, b7=0x32=50 stay static labels.
//   - RHCM 029A b2 = GENERAL BRAKE-APPLIED flag (0/1, front OR rear). *** DOWNGRADE 2026-07-29 r1
//     (adversarial QA): FRONT-SPECIFICITY REFUTED. *** b2 is a real, zero-anchored brake-applied
//     flag (r=0.99 s28 n=11 / 1.00 s44 n=8 vs broadcast front_brake_press; holds rest through
//     charge s48 = not a session artifact), but it is NOT front-specific. In s57 the lone b2=1
//     sample (t=57.4 s) coincides with a REAR-only brake: 0x133 D4=0x10 (rear pressed, within
//     0.41 s) while front pressure=0 (0x324 within 0.11 s) and the front lever=0 (0x15A D6=0). A
//     rear-only brake set b2 - so the earlier "RIGHT-hand module => right-hand front lever"
//     physical story does not hold; it flags EITHER brake. (Front-specificity DID survive for a
//     DIFFERENT signal - 0x128 D6 stays front-specific: 14 rear-only samples in s57 with D6 off.
//     Leave 0x128 D6 as-is.) [METHODOLOGY: before labeling a flag "front-X" require a matched
//     X-only counter-event (here a rear-only brake), not just an X-present correlation.] 029B
//     carries a small brake-linked sub-field (b2:b3 ~558-564, +/-6 ct) alongside its constant
//     ~1753/1754 reference-rail ADC = candidate. (The LEFT LHCM 029B/029C brake correlation is
//     a REJECTED collinear artifact - wrong hand.)
//   - VSC 0203 b2 = COARSE vehicle speed (~broadcast speed_raw / 10.1): r=1.000 vs broadcast
//     speed on s28 AND s44, 0 at standstill (parked + all charge sessions). Real but REDUNDANT
//     (a 4th speed copy after VSC 020C fine speed, EHCU 020F per-wheel, EHCU 0200 b0-1 head).
//   Full decoded catalogue: docs/livewire_s2_CAN_uds_data_map.md.
